[00:31.28]That's because you allowed your analytical brain to wake up first.|那是因为你让你的「分析型大脑」先醒了过来。
[00:35.62]In the first 10 minutes of the day,|在一天的头 10 分钟里，
[00:37.56]your brain is in a semi-conscious state called the hypnopompic state.|大脑处于一种半清醒状态，叫做 hypnopompic state（半醒状态）。
[00:42.52]Your logic is low, but your neuroplasticity is incredibly high.|这时你的逻辑能力很低，但神经可塑性却高得惊人。
[00:47.28]This is the golden window.|这就是黄金窗口期。
[00:48.92]If you wait until you are fully awake and logical,|如果你等到完全清醒、逻辑上线，
[00:52.02]your brain will start translating.|大脑就会开始翻译。
[00:53.96]It will start analyzing grammar.|开始分析语法。
[00:55.82]It will become its own worst enemy.|变成自己最大的敌人。
[00:58.28]We want to hijack this state.|我们要「劫持」这个状态，
[01:00.80]We want to bypass the translation barrier|绕过翻译这道屏障，
[01:03.36]before your logic kicks in.|趁你的逻辑还没上线。
[01:05.66]We're shifting the perspective.|我们要转换视角。
[01:07.48]English isn't an academic subject you study at 2 p.m.|英语不是下午两点才学的学科，
[01:11.44]English is a physical motor skill,|它是一项身体运动技能，
[01:13.60]like stretching or brushing your teeth,|就像伸展身体或刷牙，
[01:15.82]that you activate at 7 a.m.|早上七点就要启动它。
[01:18.16]By treating English as a physical reflex early|把英语当成一种身体反射、在清晨就启动，
[01:21.18]in the morning, you reduce the cognitive load|能减轻这之后一整天的
[01:23.96]for the rest of the day.|认知负担。
[01:25.28]You are priming the engine before the car|你是在车还没出车库前
[01:27.96]even leaves the driveway.|就先给引擎预热。
[01:29.60]If you're ready to turn your morning coffee|如果你想让早晨那杯咖啡
[01:31.68]into a fluency power-up, hit that subscribe button.|变成流利度的加成，就点个订阅吧。
[01:34.90]Let's start waking up those vocal instruments.|我们来把发声器官唤醒。
[01:37.62]Lucas, when I wake up, my voice is deep, my jaw is tight,|Lucas，我醒来时声音发闷、下巴发紧，
[01:41.34]and I can barely speak my own language, let alone English.|连母语都说不利索，更别说英语了。
[01:45.30]How do we fix that?|这怎么解决？
[01:46.84]We start with rhythmic humming.|我们从有节奏的哼唱开始。
[01:49.32]Before you even say a word, you need|在你开口之前，你需要
[01:51.54]to wake up the vocal cords for non-native phonemes.|先为非母语音素唤醒声带。
[01:55.24]Why humming?|为什么是哼唱？
[01:56.82]Humming creates a low-impact vibration that warms up the laryngeal muscles.|哼唱产生的低频振动能温和地热身喉部肌肉。
[02:02.04]But we don't just hum any tune.|但我们不是随便哼个曲子，
[02:04.30]We hum the English stress pattern.|我们哼的是英语的重音模式。
[02:07.22]I can feel that vibrating in my chest and my nose.|我能感觉到它在胸腔和鼻腔里共振。
[02:11.06]That's the American resonance.|这就是美式共鸣。
[02:13.70]Most students have stiff speech in the morning|大多数学生早上说话发僵，
[02:16.14]because their jaw and tongue are physically cold.|因为下巴和舌头在生理上是「冷」的，
[02:19.50]They haven't been moved in eight hours.|已经八个小时没动过了。
[02:22.08]We need physical warmth.|我们需要生理上的热身。
[02:23.66]I like to do jaw circles while the coffee is brewing.|我喜欢在煮咖啡的时候做下巴绕环。
[02:26.82]Exactly. Move your jaw in wide circles. Stretch your tongue to your palate, and then transition|没错。大幅度绕动下巴，把舌头伸向上颚，然后过渡到
[02:34.04]from pure sound to nonsense syllables. These syllables don't mean anything, so your brain|从单纯的声音到「无意义音节」。这些音节没有任何含义，所以大脑
[02:40.24]can't translate them. You are purely focusing on the muscles.|没法翻译它们。你纯粹在关注肌肉。
[02:44.38]It's like a runner stretching their hand strings. You are priming the tongue for the|就像跑步的人拉伸肌腱。你在为舌头做预备，
[02:48.86]specific flaps and clicks of American stress patterns.|适应美式重音模式里特有的弹舌和爆破音。
[02:52.78]If you do this for just three minutes, you'll find that when you finally do speak English,|只要做三分钟，你会发现真正开口说英语时，
[02:57.72]the words feel slippery and easy, rather than sticky and hard.|单词会变得顺滑轻松，而不是又黏又硬。
[03:02.44]Now that the muscles are warm, we need to feed them the right fuel.|肌肉热起来了，接下来要给它们喂对的燃料。
[03:07.02]And that fuel is not words, it's lexical chunks.|而那燃料不是单词，是词块（lexical chunks）。
[03:11.42]We've talked about this before, but in the morning, it's even more critical.|我们以前聊过，但早上做这件事更关键。
[03:15.66]You should have a list of five high-frequency collocations stuck to your bathroom mirror.|你该把五个高频搭配的清单贴在浴室镜子上。
[03:21.42]book, table, chair, I'm talking about nerve memory clusters. I was just about to. As far as I know,|「book, table, chair, I'm talking about...」（注：此处两位说话人声音交叠，转写有混扰）
[03:30.56]I'll look into it. You repeat these three-word clusters while you're doing a physical task,|「I'll look into it.」一边做体力活，一边重复这些三词组合，
