[03:51.12]You repeat it until it becomes an unconscious physical reflex.|一直重复到它变成无意识的身体反射。
[03:55.44]You aren't choosing the words.|你不再是在挑词，
[03:57.26]Your mouth is just executing the pattern.|嘴巴只是在执行那个模式。
[04:00.24]We use rhythmic pacing here.|这里我们用节奏节拍。
[04:02.48]Tap the side of the sink.|敲一敲洗手池边。
[04:04.14]I'll look into it.|「I'll look into it.」
[04:06.04]I'll look into it.|「I'll look into it.」
[04:08.18]This internalizes the bounce of native prosody.|这会把母语者韵律的起伏内化进去。
[04:12.02]You are teaching your body that English isn't a flat line.|你在教自己的身体：英语不是一条平线，
[04:15.34]It's a rhythmic wave.|而是有节奏的波浪。
[04:17.36]By the time you finish your morning routine, you should have fired these five chunks at least 50 times each.|等早间流程结束，这五个词块每个至少要触发过 50 次。
[04:23.68]That's 250 reps of perfect American rhythm before you've even had breakfast.|也就是早饭前就完成了 250 次完美美式节奏的重复。
[04:29.62]Now let's talk about habit stacking.|现在来聊「习惯叠加」。
[04:32.46]Lucas, you're the expert on this.|Lucas，你是这方面的专家。
[04:34.78]Habit stacking is the science of tying a new habit, English, to an existing physical movement, making coffee.|习惯叠加，就是把新习惯（英语）绑定到已有的身体动作上（煮咖啡）的科学。
[04:42.70]So the rule is, when the coffee machine starts, the English starts.|所以规则是：咖啡机一响，英语就开始。
[04:46.72]Exactly. You create a fluency bubble. For those 20 minutes, no native language is allowed.|没错。你创造一个「流利气泡」。那 20 分钟里，不许说母语。
[04:54.64]You check your 2026 AI news feeds in English. You narrate your daily schedule in English.|你用英语看 AI 新闻，用英语口述当天的日程。
[05:01.02]Okay, the machine is heating up. I need to grab my mug. Where did I put the sugar?|「好，机器在加热了，我得去拿杯子。糖放哪儿了？」
[05:06.24]This is crucial because it protects your linguistic momentum.|这很关键，因为它能保护你的语言动能。
[05:10.34]If you start your day in English, your internal monologue stays in English.|如果你用英语开始一天，你的内心独白就会停在英语里。
[05:14.56]If you start in your native language and try to switch to English at 9am, you have to fight against the inertia of your brain.|如果先用母语开始、九点再切英语，你就得对抗大脑的惯性。
[05:22.62]But if you anchor it to your morning tasks, the inertia is already on your side.|但如果把它锚定在早间任务上，惯性就站在你这边了。
[05:27.18]You are already in the zone before the stressors of the workday.|在工作日的压力到来之前，你已经进入状态了。
